course: dictionary
lesson: 1024
title: A bookcase holds books
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A bookcase is a thing you can see and touch. Its meaning is clear from what it does: it is a case for books, with shelves to hold them.
explain: «Dad builds a bookcase without reading the instructions, and it wobbles.» The clues are builds and wobbles. A bookcase is made from parts, and if it is not put together properly, it moves about unsteadily. Try your meaning in the sentence: a piece of furniture with shelves for books. It still makes sense.
explain: «A girl in Texas climbed a tall bookcase to reach a toy; it tipped over onto her.» The clues are climbed, tipped over and trapped. A tall bookcase can fall over, so context teaches us a safety lesson too.
fact: A bookcase is a piece of furniture with shelves for keeping books on.
fact: You can find bookcases at home, in classrooms and in libraries.
fact: Books on a bookcase are often sorted by size, author or subject.
fact: A tall bookcase should be fixed to the wall so it cannot tip over if a child climbs it.
fact: Useful phrases: «tall bookcase», «on the bookcase», «a built-in bookcase».
exercise: «Dad builds a bookcase without reading the instructions, and it wobbles.» What is a bookcase? | A tool for fixing walls | A shop that sells books | *A piece of furniture with shelves for keeping books on | A small box for storing toys
exercise: Where might you find a bookcase? | *In a library | Inside a loaf of bread | High in the sky | Under the sea
exercise: «A girl in Texas climbed a tall bookcase to reach a toy.» What is the safest way to set up a tall bookcase? | Stack books on top and climb to reach them | Put toys on the top shelf so children can reach them | Let it stand loose in the middle of the room | *Fix it to the wall so it cannot tip over
test: Why should a tall bookcase be fixed to the wall? | To make the room look bigger | To keep the books warm | *To stop it tipping over onto someone | To make it easier to paint the wall
test: In the phrase «a built-in bookcase», what does built-in tell you? | It is made of paper | It can be folded up and carried away | It is only for toys | *It is fixed in place, as part of the room
exam: Which of these is a bookcase? | A soft chair for reading | A bag for carrying books to school | *A piece of furniture with shelves for keeping books on | A box for keeping pencils in
